  "title": "How to Install Git On Mac - GeeksforGeeks",
  "content": "<div class=\"html-chunk\"><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>Git is an essential tool in modern software development. It helps developers track code changes, manage different versions, and work together without conflicts. Whether you are working on personal projects or team projects, Git helps keep your code organized and safe.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Why Git Matters:</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Tracks code changes and allows you to restore previous versions easily.</span></li><li value=\"2\"><span>Helps teams collaborate smoothly by managing code updates and preventing conflicts.</span></li></ul><h2 id=\"installing-git-on-macos-3-methods\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Installing Git on macOS: 3 Methods</strong></b></h2><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>You can download Git on macOS by using five different ways, so here are the commands you can run in the terminal to install it:</span></p><h3 id=\"method-1-install-git-on-macos-from-the-app-store\" style=\"text-align:left\"><span>Method 1: Install Git on macOS from the App Store</span></h3><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><span>Some users may prefer installing Git via the&nbsp;Mac App Store. Here’s how:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1: Browse for Official App store</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Open&nbsp;Mac App Store&nbsp;from any web browser and select your region.</span></li></ul><div class=\"wp-caption alignnone\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px auto; padding: 4px; border: 0px; font-size: 18px; vertical-align: baseline; max-width: 100%; text-align: center; color: rgb(39, 50, 57); font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.162px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; width: 810px;\"><img alt=\"apple2\" height=\"400\" src=\"./images/devops-154-img-1.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173516480528/apple2.webp 791w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173516480528/apple2-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173516480528/apple2-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173516480528/apple2-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173516480528/apple2-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173516480528/apple2-768.webp 768w\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px !important; margin-right: auto; margin-bottom: 0px !important; margin-left: auto; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 18px; vertical-align: baseline; height: auto; object-fit: contain; display: block; max-width: 100%; max-height: 300px !important; float: unset !important; width: auto; cursor: -webkit-zoom-in !important;\" width=\"791\"><p class=\"wp-caption-text\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px 0px 10px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 12px; vertical-align: baseline; font-style: italic; line-height: 2; color: rgb(102, 102, 102); text-align: center;\">Official Website</p></div><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2: Look up for “GIT” and click to download</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Search for&nbsp;“Git”.Select an app (e.g.,&nbsp;GitUp&nbsp;or other Git GUI tools) that includes Git and follow the installation instructions.</span></li></ul><div class=\"wp-caption alignnone\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px auto; padding: 4px; border: 0px; font-size: 18px; vertical-align: baseline; max-width: 100%; text-align: center; color: rgb(39, 50, 57); font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.162px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; width: 810px;\"><img alt=\"apple33\" height=\"556\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-154-img-2.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173719624171/apple33.webp 628w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173719624171/apple33-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173719624171/apple33-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206173719624171/apple33-300.webp 300w\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px !important; margin-right: auto; margin-bottom: 0px !important; margin-left: auto; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 18px; vertical-align: baseline; height: auto; object-fit: contain; display: block; max-width: 100%; max-height: 300px !important; float: unset !important; width: auto; cursor: -webkit-zoom-in !important;\" width=\"628\"><p class=\"wp-caption-text\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px 0px 10px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 12px; vertical-align: baseline; font-style: italic; line-height: 2; color: rgb(102, 102, 102); text-align: center;\">Click to download</p></div><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3: Verify the Extraction</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Verify the installation by running:</span></li></ul><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>git --version</span></p></blockquote><div class=\"wp-caption alignnone\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px auto; padding: 4px; border: 0px; font-size: 18px; vertical-align: baseline; max-width: 100%; text-align: center; color: rgb(39, 50, 57); font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: 0.162px; orphans: 2; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; width: 810px;\"><img alt=\"verify3\" height=\"187\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-154-img-3.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172846695430/verify3.webp 800w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172846695430/verify3-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172846695430/verify3-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172846695430/verify3-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172846695430/verify3-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172846695430/verify3-768.webp 768w\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px !important; margin-right: auto; margin-bottom: 0px !important; margin-left: auto; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 18px; vertical-align: baseline; height: auto; object-fit: contain; display: block; max-width: 100%; max-height: 300px !important; float: unset !important; width: auto; cursor: -webkit-zoom-in !important;\" width=\"800\"><p class=\"wp-caption-text\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px 0px 10px; padding: 0px; border: 0px; font-size: 12px; vertical-align: baseline; font-style: italic; line-height: 2; color: rgb(102, 102, 102); text-align: center;\">Verify</p></div><h3 id=\"method-1-install-git-on-mac-using-homebrew\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Method 2: Install GIT On Mac using Homebrew</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1: Get Homebrew in your macOS</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>If you don't have Homebrew, then type the following command in the terminal:</span></li></ul><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>/bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\"</span></p></blockquote><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"git-11\" height=\"559\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-154-img-4.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170720500989/git-11.webp 764w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170720500989/git-11-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170720500989/git-11-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170720500989/git-11-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170720500989/git-11-660.webp 660w\" width=\"764\"><figcaption>Terminal</figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2: Install Brew</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>We recommend you </span><a href=\"#/article/python/python-580\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>install Homebrew</span></a><span> first and then run the below command to download Git with no errors: </span></li></ul><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>brew install git</span></p></blockquote><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"git-22\" height=\"155\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-154-img-5.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170936364919/git-22.webp 1060w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170936364919/git-22-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170936364919/git-22-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170936364919/git-22-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170936364919/git-22-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170936364919/git-22-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206170936364919/git-22-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1060\"><figcaption>brew install</figcaption></figure><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 3: Verify the Installation</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Once the installation is complete, verify the installation:</span></li></ul><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>git --version</span></p></blockquote><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"git-33\" height=\"155\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-154-img-6.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206171410024038/git-33.webp 1060w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206171410024038/git-33-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206171410024038/git-33-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206171410024038/git-33-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206171410024038/git-33-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206171410024038/git-33-768.webp 768w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206171410024038/git-33-1024.webp 1024w\" width=\"1060\"><figcaption>Verify</figcaption></figure><h3 id=\"method-1-install-git-on-mac-using-xcode-command-line-tools\" style=\"text-align:left\"><b><strong>Method 3: Install Git on Mac using Xcode Command Line Tools</strong></b></h3><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>macOS comes with </span><a href=\"#/article/devops/devops-471\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span>Xcode Command Line Tools</span></a><span>, which includes Git and other development utilities. Here's how to install Git via Xcode:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 1: Launch Terminal  &amp; Type the following command</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>Launch Terminal by pressing CMD+Space and then type Terminal to start.</span></li></ul><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"term\" height=\"592\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-154-img-7.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172156792066/term.webp 411w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172156792066/term-100.webp 69w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172156792066/term-200.webp 139w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241206172156792066/term-300.webp 208w\" width=\"411\"><figcaption>Terminal</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span> Now, type the following command:</span></li></ul><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>xcode-select --install</span></p></blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong>Step 2: Continue with the Installation</strong></b></p><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>This will prompt you to install the Command Line Tools. Click Install to continue. Once the installations complete, verify Git by typing:</span></li></ul><blockquote><p dir=\"ltr\"><span>git --version</span></p></blockquote><figure class=\"image\"><img alt=\"verify3\" height=\"187\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"./images/devops-154-img-8.webp\" srcset=\"https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241213190545266460/verify3.webp 800w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241213190545266460/verify3-100.webp 100w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241213190545266460/verify3-200.webp 200w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241213190545266460/verify3-300.webp 300w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241213190545266460/verify3-660.webp 660w,https://media.geeksforgeeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20241213190545266460/verify3-768.webp 768w\" width=\"800\"><figcaption>verify</figcaption></figure><ul><li value=\"1\"><span>If Git is installed correctly, you will see the version number.</span></li></ul></div>",
  "textContent": "Git is an essential tool in modern software development. It helps developers track code changes, manage different versions, and work together without conflicts. Whether you are working on personal projects or team projects, Git helps keep your code organized and safe.Why Git Matters:Tracks code changes and allows you to restore previous versions easily.Helps teams collaborate smoothly by managing code updates and preventing conflicts.Installing Git on macOS: 3 MethodsYou can download Git on macOS by using five different ways, so here are the commands you can run in the terminal to install it:Method 1: Install Git on macOS from the App StoreSome users may prefer installing Git via the Mac App Store. Here’s how:Step 1: Browse for Official App storeOpen Mac App Store from any web browser and select your region.Official WebsiteStep 2: Look up for “GIT” and click to downloadSearch for “Git”.Select an app (e.g., GitUp or other Git GUI tools) that includes Git and follow the installation instructions.Click to downloadStep 3: Verify the ExtractionVerify the installation by running:git --versionVerifyMethod 2: Install GIT On Mac using HomebrewStep 1: Get Homebrew in your macOSIf you don't have Homebrew, then type the following command in the terminal:/bin/bash -c \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/HEAD/install.sh)\"TerminalStep 2: Install BrewWe recommend you install Homebrew first and then run the below command to download Git with no errors: brew install gitbrew installStep 3: Verify the InstallationOnce the installation is complete, verify the installation:git --versionVerifyMethod 3: Install Git on Mac using Xcode Command Line ToolsmacOS comes with Xcode Command Line Tools, which includes Git and other development utilities. Here's how to install Git via Xcode:Step 1: Launch Terminal  & Type the following commandLaunch Terminal by pressing CMD+Space and then type Terminal to start.Terminal Now, type the following command:xcode-select --installStep 2: Continue with the InstallationThis will prompt you to install the Command Line Tools. Click Install to continue. Once the installations complete, verify Git by typing:git --versionverifyIf Git is installed correctly, you will see the version number.",
